  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "The population of an ant colony can be modelled using the equation\n\n$$P=Ae^{kt},$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $k$ are positive constants and $t$ is time in weeks. Initially, the population is 1000. Two weeks later, the population has increased to become 1500.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of $A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=1000$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1000&=Ae^{k(0)}\\\\1000&=A.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $k=\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)$, using $P=1500$ at $t=2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1500&=1000e^{2k}\\\\e^{2k}&=\\frac32\\\\2k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right)\\\\k&=\\frac12\\ln\\left(\\frac32\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the population after four weeks?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "2,250 ants",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(4)&=1000e^{4(\\frac12\\ln(3/2))}\\\\P(4)&=1000\\left(\\frac32\\right)^2\\\\P(4)&=2250.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe population is 2,250 ants.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "After how many weeks will the population exceed 1 million? Give your answer to the nearest week.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "About 34 weeks. The population exceeds 1 million for times greater than the crossing time of approximately $34.07$ weeks.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1000e^{kt}&>1\\,000\\,000\\\\e^{kt}&>1000\\\\kt&>\\ln(1000)\\\\t&>\\frac{2\\ln(1000)}{\\ln(3/2)}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe crossing time is approximately $34.07$ weeks, which rounds to 34 weeks. The population exceeds 1 million after the crossing.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
